// t_7cc742ed.  Measured against sce-cgc 475.
// *** THE CELL THAT PROVES THE BODY CHANGED, not merely that we accept more. ***
// With the whitespace rule this is OBJECT-like with body "(x) (2.0)".  The
// reference expands it and only then fails, on the undefined x:
//     error C1008: undefined variable "x"
// We also fail INSIDE the expanded text.  What must never come back is
// "undeclared identifier 'K'" - that was the old behaviour and it means the
// macro was never defined at all.  The row asserts the refusal does NOT name
// K, which is the only way to tell the two refusals apart by verdict alone.
#define K (x) (2.0)
float4 main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { return t * K; }
